# CONFIG_UEVENT is not set
# CONFIG_WALL is not set
# CONFIG_WATCHDOG is not set
# CONFIG_FLASHCP is not set
# Third pass: the last ~20 KB needed to cross under 512 KB.
#
# order 8 charges 1048576 bytes for a 544768-byte process -- 48% of the RAM
# each process holds is waste. Dropping under 524288 makes the allocator
# charge 524288 instead, which doubles how many processes fit. A 3.6% size
# cut buys a 2x capacity win, so it is worth being fussy about.
#
# These are the Process Utilities nobody needs when ps, top, kill, killall,
# pidof, uptime and free all stay. dd goes too (cat covers it here), and
# MKE2FS is the symbol that actually controls mkfs.ext2 -- disabling
# CONFIG_MKFS_EXT2 alone left mkfs_ext2_main linked in.
